# herdr plugins, installed by setup.sh's `extensions` step.
#
# One owner/repo per line, as `herdr plugin install` takes it. `#` comments and
# blank lines are ignored.
#
# setup.sh installed two of these as literal command lines; three are installed
# on macbook-m5-pro. ogulcancelik/herdr-browser was the missing one, so a fresh
# machine silently came up without it.
#
# Note that the installed plugin id is not the repo name: herdr reports these as
# cloudmanic.herdr-plus and tdi.worktree-setup respectively, which is why a
# directory listing under config/herdr/plugins/github/ cannot be used to
# reconstruct this list.
#
# ogulcancelik/herdr-browser is deliberately absent although the plugin
# (official.browser) is installed and wired into config.toml's quick actions.
# Upstream deprecated it on 2026-08-28 and deleted herdr-plugin.toml from HEAD,
# so `herdr plugin install` — which is also the update path — now fails with a
# bare ENOENT and broke `bin/update` on every run. The installed copy at
# be6888b7 keeps working. The successor is zenbu-labs/terminal-browser, whose
# manifest lives in a herdr-plugin/ subdir, so the install argument is
# zenbu-labs/terminal-browser/herdr-plugin rather than the bare repo. Its
# min_herdr_version is 0.8.2, which config/mise/mise.toml now satisfies, but its
# build step is a curl-into-bash installer — so adopting it is a deliberate
# choice, plus swapping the config.toml quick action to
# zenbu-labs.terminal-browser.

cloudmanic/herdr-plus
tdi/herdr-worktree-setup
